### Case: dot-dot-path — "../" segments, sent as-is.
###
### Expect 404 {"error_msg":"404 Route Not Found"}. Send it with
### curl --path-as-is "{{GATEWAY}}/v1/customers/../../users/1/todos" — most
### clients, curl included, resolve the "../" themselves before sending.
GET {{GATEWAY}}/v1/customers/../../users/1/todos
accept: application/json
